# Project Binder — core

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the module map. Do not invent parallel architecture.

## Code shape

- **Reuse first**: check `src/utils.js`, `src/db*.js`, `src/api.js`, and existing components before adding helpers or UI shells.
- **Extract on the second copy** — especially in `App.jsx` and `Board.jsx`. Prefer a small shared file over growing megacomponents with paste.
- Match existing React style (function components, no new state library, no new CSS framework).
- Don’t add dependencies unless clearly needed for the task.
- Don’t “clean up” unrelated code while implementing a feature.
- Prefer file-private helpers; avoid exporting symbols only used in one file.
- Comments: invariants / non-obvious why only — never narrate the next line.

## Workspace mutations

```text
API call (src/api.js) → applyWorkspace(data, opts) in App
```

- Prefer `keepNav(projectSlug, boardSlug)` from App so project/tab/`g` survive reload.
- Do not introduce a second client store for workspace data.

## Agent defaults

- Commit / push / amend / browser QA only when the user asks.
- Verify with `npm run build` (or existing checks) after substantive edits.
